    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Determine which of $\\frac{4}{5}$ or $\\frac{5}{6}$ is larger.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{5}{6}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{4}{5}&=\\frac{24}{30}\\\\\\frac{5}{6}&=\\frac{25}{30}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $25>24$, $\\frac{5}{6}$ is larger.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "We generalise the above result as follows. Suppose that $n>1$. By writing the left-hand side as a single fraction, prove that\n$$\\frac{n}{n+1}-\\frac{n-1}{n}>0.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$$\\frac{n}{n+1}-\\frac{n-1}{n}=\\frac{1}{n(n+1)}>0.$$\n\nThe numerator is positive and, since $n>1$, so is the denominator.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{n}{n+1}-\\frac{n-1}{n}&=\\frac{n^2}{n(n+1)}-\\frac{(n-1)(n+1)}{n(n+1)}\\\\\\frac{n}{n+1}-\\frac{n-1}{n}&=\\frac{n^2-(n^2-1)}{n(n+1)}\\\\\\frac{n}{n+1}-\\frac{n-1}{n}&=\\frac{1}{n(n+1)}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $n>1$, $n(n+1)>0$. Therefore $\\frac{n}{n+1}-\\frac{n-1}{n}>0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
  },
